[Skia] ShareableBitmap::createGraphicsContext() dereferences a null SkSurface

SkSurfaces::WrapPixels() returns nullptr when the pixel geometry is not
something Skia can raster into: SkSurfaceValidateRasterInfo() refuses an
empty size and, more to the point here, any image whose
height * rowBytes exceeds SK_MaxS32 (SkSurface_Raster.cpp). createGraphicsContext()
then calls surface->getCanvas() on the null pointer and the web process
dies with SIGSEGV.

This is reachable from the public API. webkit_web_view_get_snapshot() with
WEBKIT_SNAPSHOT_REGION_FULL_DOCUMENT sizes the bitmap from
LocalFrameView::contentsSize() times the device scale factor
(WebPage::takeSnapshot); Epiphany asks for exactly that for its overview
thumbnails one second after every top-site load. A long Wikipedia article
laid out 2802 px wide comes to 237522 px tall on a phone: 2802 * 4 * 237522
is 2.66 GB, SharedMemory::allocate() happily hands out the memfd, Skia says
no, and the process crashes. Observed twice in a row on webkitgtk 2.52.6
(aarch64, GTK4, Skia CPU rendering), coredump symbolized:

    #0 getCachedCanvas               SkSurface_Base.h:208
    #1 SkSurface::getCanvas          SkSurface.cpp:83
    #2 ShareableBitmap::createGraphicsContext  ShareableBitmapSkia.cpp:68
    #3 ImageBufferShareableBitmapBackend::create
    #4 WebChromeClient::createImageBuffer
    #5 WebImage::create
    #6 WebPage::snapshotAtSize        WebPage.cpp:3282
    #7 WebPage::takeSnapshot          WebPage.cpp:3150

Check the surface. On failure Skia does not invoke the release proc, so the
ref() taken for it has to be dropped by hand or the bitmap -- and its shared
memory -- leaks. Every caller already handles a null GraphicsContext:
ImageBufferShareableBitmapBackend::create() returns nullptr and
WebImage::create() falls back to createEmpty(), so the snapshot request
completes with an empty image instead of taking the page down.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/ShareableBitmapSkia.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/skia/ShareableBitmapSkia.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,12 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsContext> ShareableBitmap::createGraphicsContext()
     auto surface = SkSurfaces::WrapPixels(m_configuration.imageInfo(), mutableSpan().data(), bytesPerRow(), [](void*, void* context) {
         static_cast<ShareableBitmap*>(context)->deref();
     }, this, &properties);
+    if (!surface) {
+        // Skia refuses geometries it cannot raster into (empty, or larger than
+        // SK_MaxS32 bytes) and does not call the release proc when it does.
+        deref();
+        return nullptr;
+    }
 
     auto* canvas = surface->getCanvas();
     if (!canvas)
